# jasmin/ECLIB_AXIOMS
# ===================
#
# Every `axiom` and every `admit` or `admitted` in the Jasmin EasyCrypt
# library (eclib/*.ec) of the tree build.sh builds, one per line: file,
# keyword, name, and `<-` when the line is not a declaration but realises
# an axiom of a cloned theory. build.sh stops if the scan differs from this
# list.
#
# There is no `admit` or `admitted`. The declared axioms are of two kinds:
#
# - Parameters of abstract theories (JArray, JByte_array, JWord,
#   JWord_array: 44 declarations). They hold in a clone of the theory once
#   the clone realises them; the `<-` lines are such realisations.
# - Global axioms: the memory model (JMemory: mem_eq_ext, get_setE,
#   allocated8_setE), the AES helpers (AES: InvSboxK, InvMixColumnsK,
#   InvMixColumnsD) and the horizontal addition of the x86-64 model
#   (JModel_x86: hadd_nil, hadd_cons2). EasyCrypt proofs about code that
#   uses them rest on them, so they are part of those proofs' trusted base.

